@startuml target_session_events_resource_model
title CampusClaw Target POST Events and History
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java 918005ee8ccc88d179fc31a0de17a92b4a01383b.
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeEventController.java,
' submit/list, lines 61-91: POST SSE and GET history; no standalone read stream.
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventService.java,
' prepareAndSubmitLocked/acceptUserEntry, lines 101-141: persist message then start.
' These files are unchanged from a8192e047f4061bd385297d3dc6c4358362d0d49.
' Observed behavior: current Java already uses request-scoped POST SSE.
' Confirmed target architecture: combine submission and output in one POST;
' the first business frame is the complete accepted user event, exactly once.
' Design reason: remove the gap between a write and an independent live subscription.
' Target-only: union input, response projection, causal ordering and fixed snapshot.
' Source evidence: campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository.java,
' acceptUserEvent: row lock, idle recheck, message append and running update in one transaction.
' Confirmed product constraint: one unfinished user.message per Session across instances.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ArrowColor #475569
}
actor "mate-service" as Mate
participant "Event Application Service\n<<target-only>>" as API
participant "Request Output Binding\n<<target-only>>" as Binding
participant "Ordered Event Appender\n<<target-only>>" as Append
database "Session Store" as Store
participant "Execution Coordinator\n<<existing-changed>>" as Execution
participant "Request SSE Writer\n<<per POST>>" as Writer

Mate -> API : POST /sessions/{sessionId}/events
API -> Binding : reserve bounded response capacity
critical Session admission and target binding
  API -> Binding : bind this message, resume segment or interrupt target
  API -> Append : validate dependencies and accept user event
  Append -> Store : short transaction: type-specific admission and append\nmessage: require idle, set running; interrupt: persist stop intent
  Store --> Append : committed user event
  Append --> API : accepted event
  API -> Binding : enqueue complete user receipt first
  API -> Execution : start / resume only; interrupt is handled by DB polling
end
Binding -> Writer : release ordered response frames
Writer --> Mate : 200 SSE; data: complete user.* receipt

loop Output belonging to the bound request scope
  alt Preview only
    Execution -> Binding : preview delta best-effort
  else Authoritative event
    Execution -> Append : authoritative event
    Append -> Store : ordered commit outside model/tool calls
    Store --> Append : committed event
    Append -> Binding : publish after commit in Session order
  end
  Binding -> Writer : response-specific immutable event
  Writer --> Mate : data: agent.* JSON
end
group Confirmed idle closing and database interrupt handoff
  Execution -> Append : corresponding idle state
  Append -> Store : commit corresponding boundary\nactual finish: set idle; confirmation wait: retain running
  Append -> Binding : publish matching session.status_idle
  Binding -> Writer : enqueue idle, then complete this response
  Writer --> Mate : data: idle; response ends
end
Mate -> API : GET /sessions/{sessionId}/events
API -> Store : query fixed snapshot in committed internal order
Store --> API : ordered complete events
API --> Mate : ResultBean JSON history

note over API,Execution
No public executionId, runId or sequence.
Credentials belong only to the required in-memory execution.
Do not hold a DB transaction while calling models, tools or network writers.
end note
note over Binding,Writer
Never broadcast unrelated Session events to this response.
A closed response does not cancel accepted execution.
History repairs uncertainty; never replay the POST automatically.
Interrupt delivery uses durable stop intent and per-instance polling.
Redis is deferred; no sticky routing or instance forwarding.
end note
note over API,Store
Reject a new user.message while M1 is unfinished; never queue it.
The busy response is sent before opening SSE.
Control events use their own admission rules.
Confirmation idle ends the HTTP response; the resource stays running.
end note
@enduml

@startuml target_session_events_classes
title CampusClaw Target Request-scoped Event Classes
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java 918005ee8ccc88d179fc31a0de17a92b4a01383b.
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventStream.java,
' attach/detachInternal, lines 93-159: bounded single-subscriber stream.
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeExecutionCoordinator.java,
' completeExecution, lines 154-168: persistence, terminal events, stream completion.
' Observed behavior: a current stream belongs to one active execution.
' Target-only architecture: per-request bindings support union input without a
' public Session subscription API. Interrupt delivery and database coordination are confirmed.
' RuntimeActiveExecution.requestAbort is local; target polling is not current behavior.
' Design reason: keep web VOs, application admission, runtime and persistence separate;
' retain independent response backpressure and shared causal append ordering.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  ArrowColor #64748B
}
top to bottom direction

package "runtimeapi.web" {
  class RuntimeEventController <<singleton, existing-changed>>
  class RuntimeSseEmitterSubscriber <<per response, existing-changed>>
}
package "runtimeapi.vo" {
  class SubmitSessionEventRequestVO <<validated request, target-only>>
  class SessionEventResponseVO <<immutable response, target-only>>
}
package "runtimeapi.application" {
  class SessionEventApplicationService <<singleton, target-only>>
  class SessionEventHandlerRegistry <<singleton, target-only>>
  interface SessionEventHandler <<target-only>>
  class UserMessageEventHandler <<singleton, target-only>>
  class UserInterruptEventHandler <<singleton, target-only>>
  class UserToolConfirmationEventHandler <<singleton, target-only>>
  class SessionEventAppender <<singleton, target-only>>
  class SessionEventQueryService <<singleton, existing-changed>>
  class SessionEventProjector <<per execution, target-only>>
}
package "runtimeapi.runtime" {
  class RuntimeExecutionCoordinator <<singleton, existing-changed>>
  class RuntimeActiveExecution <<per execution, existing-changed>>
}
package "runtimeapi.event" {
  class RequestEventRouter <<singleton, target-only>>
  class RequestOutputBinding <<per request, target-only>>
  class RequestEventStream <<per response, target-only>>
}
package "runtimeapi.persistence" {
  interface RuntimeSessionRepository <<existing-changed>>
  class MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository <<singleton, existing-changed>>
}
package "runtimeapi.dto" {
  class RuntimeEntryDTO <<database data, existing-changed>>
  class ExecutionTargetDTO <<immutable internal identity, target-only>>
}

RuntimeEventController --> SubmitSessionEventRequestVO : validates
RuntimeEventController --> SessionEventApplicationService : submit
RuntimeEventController --> SessionEventQueryService : list
RuntimeEventController --> RuntimeSseEmitterSubscriber : starts writer
RuntimeSseEmitterSubscriber --> SessionEventResponseVO : serializes
RuntimeSseEmitterSubscriber --> RequestEventStream : drains
SessionEventApplicationService --> SessionEventHandlerRegistry : selects handler
SessionEventHandlerRegistry o-- "3" SessionEventHandler
SessionEventHandler <|.. UserMessageEventHandler
SessionEventHandler <|.. UserInterruptEventHandler
SessionEventHandler <|.. UserToolConfirmationEventHandler
SessionEventHandler --> SessionEventAppender : recheck and accept
UserMessageEventHandler --> RuntimeExecutionCoordinator : start
UserToolConfirmationEventHandler --> RuntimeExecutionCoordinator : resume
SessionEventApplicationService --> RequestEventRouter : reserve and bind before action
RuntimeExecutionCoordinator *-- "0..1 per Session" RuntimeActiveExecution
SessionEventApplicationService *-- "0..*" SessionEventProjector : owns subscriptions
SessionEventProjector ..> RuntimeActiveExecution : observes normalized events
SessionEventProjector --> SessionEventAppender : ordered authoritative append
SessionEventAppender --> RuntimeSessionRepository : short transaction
SessionEventAppender --> RequestEventRouter : committed event, ordered
SessionEventProjector --> RequestEventRouter : preview
RequestEventRouter *-- "0..*" RequestOutputBinding
RequestOutputBinding --> "1" ExecutionTargetDTO : fixed target, not a remote Java object
RuntimeActiveExecution --> "1" ExecutionTargetDTO : local identity
RequestOutputBinding *-- "1" RequestEventStream
RequestEventStream o-- "0..*" SessionEventResponseVO : bounded queue
SessionEventQueryService --> RuntimeSessionRepository
RuntimeSessionRepository <|.. MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository
MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository --> RuntimeEntryDTO

note right of RequestOutputBinding
Message / resume segment or interrupt target.
Never resolve the latest active execution on every event.
Interrupt bindings can refer to executions on another instance.
No raw credentials or public execution identifier.
end note
note bottom of SessionEventAppender
All writers share causal prerequisite checks and ordered commit.
Message admission locks the Session and rechecks idle in the DB.
Append the message and set running together; reject new messages while busy.
Interrupt event and stop intent commit together for a fixed target.
Terminal event and target result link also commit atomically.
Allocate sequence and append atomically, retaining lock to commit.
Network and model/tool work stay outside the transaction.
Implementation names and scheduling remain target-only.
end note
note bottom of RequestEventStream
Receipt first, exactly once; then matching output.
Slow clients fail independently without cancelling execution.
DTOs never cross the HTTP response boundary.
end note
@enduml

@startuml target_session_live_stream_lifecycle
title CampusClaw POST SSE - Closing and Interrupt Delivery Confirmed
' Stable block name retained for existing SVG links; this is no longer a GET stream.
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java 918005ee8ccc88d179fc31a0de17a92b4a01383b.
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeTerminalEventFactory.java,
' emit, lines 34-57: current idle plus stream.end, or stream.error on failure.
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeSseEmitterSubscriber.java,
' onEvent/onComplete, lines 33-49: named SSE; explicit emitter completion.
' Confirmed: one POST for input/output, user receipt first, data-only and type+phase.
' Confirmed target-only: matching idle ends this response, including confirmation waits.
' Design reason: do not keep a completed request open for unrelated later messages.
' Confirmed: original output stays on A; B receives receipt and the same stop idle only.
' Confirmed target-only: durable DB stop requests and per-instance batch polling; no Redis.
' Exact schema, polling interval, races, idle reason literals and failures remain open.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ArrowColor #475569
}
actor "mate-service" as Client
participant "POST Events API\n<<target-only>>" as API
participant "Bound Execution\n<<internal>>" as Execution
participant "Response A\n<<per request>>" as A
participant "Response B\n<<per request>>" as B
participant "Local Control Poller\n<<per instance, target-only>>" as Poller
database "History and Control Store" as Store

Client -> API : POST user.message
API -> A : reserve and bind before starting execution
API -> Store : short transaction: lock Session, require idle,\nappend M1 and set running
API -> A : complete user.message receipt first
API -> Execution : start only after receipt is queued
A --> Client : data: user.message receipt
Execution -> A : matching agent events
A --> Client : data: agent.* output

opt Another user.message arrives while M1 is unfinished
  Client -> API : POST user.message M2
  API -> Store : check authoritative admission state
  Store --> API : busy; no message appended
  API --> Client : reject before SSE\n409 SESSION_BUSY (candidate error)
end

alt Confirmed: close on matching execution idle
  Execution -> Store : actual exit; commit done / failed boundary\nand set matching Session idle
  Execution -> A : corresponding idle, then complete
  A --> Client : data: session.status_idle; EOF
else Confirmed: close while waiting for tool confirmation
  Execution -> Store : commit Tool Call and confirming boundary\nretain Session running; M1 is unfinished
  Execution -> A : tool call, confirming idle, then complete
  A --> Client : data: tool call; data: confirming idle; EOF
  Client -> API : new POST user.tool_confirmation
  API -> B : atomically bind valid pending tool and resume segment
  API -> Store : accept and persist confirmation
  API -> B : complete confirmation receipt first
  API -> Execution : resume
  B --> Client : data: user.tool_confirmation receipt
  Execution -> Store : actual exit after resume; commit terminal\nand set matching Session idle
  Execution -> B : tool result, response, corresponding idle
  B --> Client : data: matching output; idle; EOF
else Confirmed delivery: interrupt while response A remains open
  Client -> API : new POST user.interrupt
  API -> B : reserve response; retain fixed internal target
  API -> Store : transaction: bind target, persist interrupt and stop intent
  API -> B : complete interrupt receipt first
  B --> Client : data: user.interrupt receipt
  Poller -> Store : batch read stop intents for local executions
  Store --> Poller : stop intent with fixed target
  Poller -> Execution : recheck identity; request local cancellation
  Execution -> Store : commit actual stop idle and target result link\nset matching Session idle
  Execution -> A : final committed idle if still attached
  API -> Store : result poll: read this target's committed idle
  Store --> API : same immutable idle event
  API -> B : same idle eventId after receipt, then complete
  A --> Client : data: terminated idle; EOF
  B --> Client : data: terminated idle; EOF
end

group Transport failure at any point
  Client -> Client : preserve uncertainty if no authoritative terminal
  note over A,B
  Detach only the failed response; do not cancel execution.
  No POST replay or independent GET stream reconnection.
  end note
  Client -> API : GET /sessions/{sessionId}/events
  API -> Store : fixed committed snapshot
  Store --> API : complete events in internal order
  API --> Client : ResultBean history
  Client -> Client : deduplicate by eventId; retain array order
end
@enduml

@startuml target_database_interrupt_delivery
title CampusClaw Target Database-backed Interrupt
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java 918005ee8ccc88d179fc31a0de17a92b4a01383b.
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeActiveExecution.java,
' requestAbort/complete: in-memory cancellation and completion only.
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeSessionEngineRegistry.java,
' register/find: active executions live inside one process.
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository.java,
' acceptUserEvent/finishExecution: current message acceptance and Session state updates.
' Observed behavior: current Java has no durable cross-instance interrupt handoff.
' Confirmed target architecture: DB stop intent and per-instance batch polling.
' Design reason: accept on any instance without sticky routing or remote Java references.
' Schema, interval, race response details and crash recovery remain under review.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ArrowColor #475569
}
actor "mate-service" as Client
participant "Instance B\nInterrupt API / Result Poller\n<<target-only>>" as B
database "Shared DB\nControl + Authoritative Events" as DB
participant "Instance A\nControl Poller\n<<target-only>>" as Poller
participant "Instance A\nExecution / Original SSE" as A

note over DB,A
The accepted execution identity is already registered in the DB.
The Session stays running until M1 actually finishes; new messages are rejected.
Its live Agent object and credentials remain on instance A.
end note
Client -> B : POST user.interrupt
B -> B : reserve bounded response capacity
group Short admission transaction
  B -> DB : lock and validate current target identity
  B -> DB : append user.interrupt and persist stop intent
  DB --> B : commit; complete receipt and fixed target
end
B -> B : enqueue receipt before any result delivery
B --> Client : interrupt SSE: complete user.interrupt receipt

Poller -> DB : batch read stop intents for local active targets
DB --> Poller : pending stop for the fixed target
Poller -> A : recheck identity and request local cancellation
A -> A : finish cancellation and execution cleanup
group Short terminal transaction
  A -> DB : recheck target; append one authoritative idle
  A -> DB : link target to idle; set only matching Session idle
  DB --> A : commit; one idle eventId
end
A --> Client : original SSE: same committed idle; close

B -> DB : batch read terminal results for local waiting responses
DB --> B : this target's already committed idle
B -> B : project immutable response VO; retain eventId
B --> Client : interrupt SSE: same idle; close

note over B,DB
B reads only the terminal result, not Agent output.
A may finish before B polls; the committed result remains readable.
No credential is stored in control records or polling queues.
end note
note over Poller,A
Polling does not wait for the next token or tool response.
Recheck the fixed generation; never cancel a later execution.
Repeated checks must not repeat side effects or block the whole batch.
end note
note over B,A
Timeout, DB failure or owner loss is not proof of successful interruption.
No automatic takeover or POST replay; reconcile authoritative history.
Polling interval, batch size and failure handling details remain open.
Redis is a future optional wake-up optimization, not a current dependency.
end note
@enduml

@startuml target_database_interrupt_classes
title CampusClaw Target Database Interrupt - Application Boundaries
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java 918005ee8ccc88d179fc31a0de17a92b4a01383b.
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeSessionEngineRegistry.java,
' register/find: active execution objects are process-local.
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository.java,
' acceptUserEvent/finishExecution: existing transaction adapter; no durable stop handoff.
' Observed behavior: current control and completion handles cannot cross JVM boundaries.
' Target-only design: every instance deploys both polling services; each owns local work only.
' Design reason: share durable identity and results, never a remote mutable Agent reference.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  ArrowColor #64748B
}
top to bottom direction
package "Application - singleton per instance, target-only" {
  class "UserInterruptEventHandler" as Accept
  class "SessionEventAppender" as Append
  class "ExecutionControlPollingService" as Control
  class "InterruptResultPollingService" as Result
}
package "Runtime - local to executing instance" {
  class "RuntimeExecutionCoordinator" as Runtime <<existing-changed>>
  class "RuntimeActiveExecution" as Execution <<per execution, existing-changed>>
}
package "Response - local to receiving instance" {
  class "RequestOutputBinding" as Binding <<per request, target-only>>
  class "RequestEventStream" as Stream <<bounded, target-only>>
  class "SessionEventResponseVO" as VO <<immutable, target-only>>
}
package "Persistence - shared database boundary" {
  interface "RuntimeSessionRepository" as Repo <<existing-changed>>
  class "MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository" as Adapter <<singleton, existing-changed>>
}
class "ExecutionTargetDTO" as Target <<immutable internal identity, target-only>>

Accept --> Append : admit\ninterrupt
Append --> Repo : atomic receipt\n+ stop intent
Control --> Repo : batch local-target\nstop requests
Control --> Runtime : snapshot targets;\nrecheck and cancel
Runtime *-- "0..1 per Session" Execution
Runtime --> Append : actual exit; commit\none terminal + result link
Result --> Repo : batch terminal results\nfor local waiters
Result --> Binding : inspect fixed\nwaiting targets
Result --> Stream : convert DTO to VO;\ndeliver same idle
Binding --> "1" Target
Execution --> "1" Target
Binding *-- "1" Stream
Stream o-- "0..*" VO
Repo <|.. Adapter

note bottom of Target
Session + execution identity only.
No remote Agent or public ID.
Recheck state at its owner.
end note
note bottom of Control
Independent of model/tool calls.
No slow cancellation in this loop.
end note
note bottom of Result
Receipt first; terminal only.
No copied Agent output.
Disconnect removes the waiter,
not the durable stop intent.
end note
@enduml
